body:
Hi @david6666666, I would like to take the open MiniMax-H3 packed SAGE_ATTN_3 follow-up in section 3.1.

The scope I plan to implement is:

- add an explicit backend capability for a packed sequence with one valid Q/K/V prefix plus structural alignment padding;
- make SAGE_ATTN_3 validate MiniMax-H3 packed metadata, run only the valid prefix, and restore the aligned output shape without allowing padding tokens to affect valid tokens;
- preserve exact fallback behavior for unsupported GQA/MQA or malformed metadata;
- add focused backend/model contract tests, documentation, and 8x B300 SM103 correctness, quality, profiling, and end-to-end performance results.

Duplicate check: PR #1975 is the HunyuanImage3 packed FlashAttention path and does not cover MiniMax-H3 or SAGE_ATTN_3. Draft PR #5852 owns the SM120 FlashInfer backend and generic 2/4/8-GPU benchmark tooling; I will not duplicate that backend or its benchmark files. I found no open PR or comment claiming the H3 packed SAGE_ATTN_3 item.

The performance PR will only be opened if the same 8x B300 workload shows a repeatable end-to-end gain and the existing MiniMax-H3 accuracy/output gates pass. Please let me know if this conflicts with work already in flight.

Follow-up on my B300 investigation: the TRTLLM packed-prefix experiment was not large enough to justify a PR, so I am not pursuing it.

I am now qualifying a different, narrowly scoped MiniMax-H3 SP-boundary optimization, extracted and reimplemented on current `main` from the independently reviewable ideas in the closed #5750 branch (with attribution to @david6666666):

- construct each strict-Ulysses rank's packed embedding/RoPE rows locally instead of materializing the full `[S, 5376]` activation on every rank and immediately discarding 7/8 of it;
- keep rows sharded through the row-local final projection, then gather `[S, 128]` FP32 logits rather than `[S, 5376]` BF16 hidden states.

This does **not** change the Ulysses Q/K/V all-to-all implementation, attention backend, or packed-prefix handling. On 8x B300, current-main `f41451f6`, TRTLLM_ATTN, U8, 1344x768 / 4s, eager, one excluded warmup + three measured requests, the initial combined implementation changed steady `diffuse` median from 0.5742s to 0.5698s (-0.77%) and peak memory from 89,652 MB to 88,554 MB per rank. Video arrays were bit-exact; audio cosine was 0.9999998 with max abs delta 1.79e-4. I am still running regional-compile and full 50-step validation, and will only open a PR if the gain remains repeatable.

@linzhenpl07, since you claimed the broader H3-specific USP communication item, please flag if your in-progress work includes these same pre/post-block boundaries. If so I will not open a duplicate; if your scope is attention-internal communication, the implementations should remain distinct.
